Baseline: lung nodule measurement on CT, a research aid
The code in this repository is under the MIT License (see LICENSE), except the optional nodule finder in finder/,
which is under the GNU Affero General Public License 3.0 (see finder/LICENSE and finder/NOTICE.md).

Research use only. Not a medical device. Baseline does not diagnose, and its measurements are not for clinical decisions.

This repository contains no model weights and no scans. The parts below are used by Baseline under their own licences.

1. nnInteractive (the outline model)
   Isensee F., Rokuss M., Kraemer L. et al. nnInteractive: Redefining 3D Promptable Segmentation. 2025. arXiv:2503.08373.
   German Cancer Research Center (DKFZ), https://github.com/MIC-DKFZ/nnInteractive
   - Code: Apache License 2.0. Installed from PyPI as a dependency (nninteractive), not copied here.
   - Model weights: Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0): non-commercial use only.
     They are downloaded from their publisher (Hugging Face, MIC-DKFZ/nnInteractive) when the tool is installed.
     They are never part of this repository.

2. Practice scans (three public patients, downloaded when the tool is installed; never part of this repository)
   From The Cancer Imaging Archive (TCIA):
   - RIDER Lung CT. Zhao B., Schwartz L. H., Kris M. G., Riely G. J. (2015). Coffee-break lung CT collection with scan
     images reconstructed at multiple imaging parameters (Version 3). The Cancer Imaging Archive.
     https://doi.org/10.7937/k9/tcia.2015.u1x8a5nr
     Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (CC BY 4.0).
   - RIDER-LungCT-Seg. Wee L., Aerts H. J. W. L., Kalendralis P., Dekker A. (2020). RIDER Lung CT Segmentation Labels
     from: Decoding tumour phenotype by noninvasive imaging using a quantitative radiomics approach [Data set].
     The Cancer Imaging Archive. https://doi.org/10.7937/tcia.2020.jit9grk8
     Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 (CC BY 3.0), as listed by TCIA and NCI Imaging Data Commons.

3. NCI Imaging Data Commons (the download path for the practice scans)
   The scans are downloaded with idc-index from NCI Imaging Data Commons, which mirrors these TCIA collections.
   https://portal.imaging.datacommons.cancer.gov
   Fedorov A. et al. National Cancer Institute Imaging Data Commons: Toward Transparency, Reproducibility, and
   Scalability in Imaging Artificial Intelligence. RadioGraphics (2023). https://doi.org/10.1148/rg.230180

4. Atkinson Hyperlegible Next (the page's typeface)
   Copyright 2020-2024 The Atkinson Hyperlegible Next Project Authors (Braille Institute of America).
   SIL Open Font License 1.1. The font files and the licence are in web/src/fonts/ (OFL.txt). The font is bundled
   with the page, so nothing is fetched from the internet.

5. The nodule finder (optional; finder/, a separate program that the engine starts as its own process)
   Its code is under AGPL-3.0 (finder/LICENSE). It is off unless it is turned on. Research use only.
   - Ultralytics: GNU Affero General Public License 3.0 (AGPL-3.0). https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics
     Installed by uv from finder/uv.lock as a dependency, not copied here.
   - The model: Chou L.-F. et al. Diagnostics 2026;16(18):3038. https://doi.org/10.3390/diagnostics16183038
     Weights: Lien-Feng/Lightweight-2-5D-LUNA16 on Hugging Face, pinned to revision d9bc7ec3f06fab778f941fd8f05de145f1a7332c.
     Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (CC BY 4.0). https://doi.org/10.57967/hf/10295
     The weights and that repository's code (luna_rev/) are downloaded from their publisher at first use. They are never
     part of this repository.
   - Training data of the model: LUNA16 (CC BY 4.0) and LIDC-IDRI (CC BY 3.0).
   - The finder's accuracy numbers: LIDC-annot-NLST501. Renoust B., Baudot P. et al. (2026). The Cancer Imaging Archive.
     https://doi.org/10.7937/Y2DX-E334. Licence: CC BY 4.0.

6. Data used only in results/ (never part of the tool's install or this repository's scans)
   - QIBA VolCT 1B: the radiologists' measurements used as a second reference. McNitt-Gray M. et al. (2020).
     The Cancer Imaging Archive. https://doi.org/10.7937/tcia.2020.1c3h-vp70
     Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (CC BY 4.0).
   - National Lung Screening Trial (NLST): the images of the 10 spiculated nodules in the known limits.
     National Lung Screening Trial Research Team. (2013). Data from the National Lung Screening Trial (NLST) [Data set].
     The Cancer Imaging Archive. https://doi.org/10.7937/TCIA.HMQ8-J677
     Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (CC BY 4.0).
   - LIDC-annot-NLST501: the readers' outlines of those nodules (see 5).

